WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:07.301
Policing teams work across controlled policy, case material, evidential
records, disclosure schedules, decision logs and supervisory

00:07.301 --> 00:07.736
reviews.

00:07.736 --> 00:16.424
Before an accountable action or recommendation is approved, the authorised
person needs the governing source, the current wording and a

00:16.424 --> 00:19.031
defensible route back to the record.

00:19.031 --> 00:22.507
Cortessa is designed to support that documentary investigation.

00:22.507 --> 00:31.196
It does not assess guilt, identify suspects, direct operations, make charging
decisions or determine what a prosecutor or court should

00:31.196 --> 00:31.630
decide.

00:32.630 --> 00:39.770
A review can depend on operational policy, local procedure, evidential
material, disclosure records, supervisory directions and earlier

00:39.770 --> 00:40.190
decisions.

00:40.190 --> 00:46.070
Each source has an owner, status, access boundary and place in the formal
process.

00:46.070 --> 00:49.430
The challenge is not simply finding matching words.

00:49.430 --> 00:57.410
It is establishing which source is current, whether every referenced record is
present, how chronology and amendments connect, and

00:57.410 --> 01:01.190
whether the route to the original material remains inspectable.

01:02.190 --> 01:09.239
Cortessa's target policing-site deployment gives each authorised investigator,
disclosure specialist, analyst or supervisor a

01:09.239 --> 01:12.764
dedicated, self-sufficient box inside the site boundary.

01:12.764 --> 01:19.310
Permitted records, ingestion, index, on-device model and source viewer remain
on that box.

01:19.310 --> 01:23.842
Audit and Ask run locally against the approved corpus.

01:23.842 --> 01:27.870
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:27.870 --> 01:36.430
The user controls the local working context and remains responsible for
interpretation, handling and every approved revision.

01:37.430 --> 01:44.118
User boxes are designed to connect through permission-scoped departmental
nodes for investigations, disclosure, professional standards

01:44.118 --> 01:47.685
and supervisory assurance, then to an on-site hub.

01:47.685 --> 01:56.156
The exchange remains inside the air-gapped site, with selected sharing only
where role, case and handling authority permit it.

01:56.156 --> 02:02.844
This is Cortessa's target site architecture, not a claim of a deployed
production network today.

02:02.844 --> 02:09.086
The governed offline revision contract and application foundations exist;
authenticated transport, key provisioning, delivery

02:09.086 --> 02:13.990
scheduling, backup, recovery, site assurance and physical rollout remain
deployment work.

02:14.990 --> 02:17.071
Audit leads the Cortessa workflow.

02:17.071 --> 02:23.315
It works across the bounded corpus rather than waiting for one question at a
time.

02:23.315 --> 02:31.223
It can surface a policy that cites a missing source, records with revision or
chronology uncertainty, inconsistent terminology, an

02:31.223 --> 02:36.634
unresolved reference or a documentary gap that may require disclosure or
supervisory attention.

02:36.634 --> 02:43.710
Each candidate is a cited question for review, not a conclusion about
evidence, misconduct, legality or guilt.

02:44.710 --> 02:50.315
Every candidate leads back to the passage or record that created it.

02:50.315 --> 02:58.723
The authorised reviewer can inspect surrounding context, document state,
chronology and the applicable access boundary before forming a

02:58.723 --> 02:59.190
judgement.

02:59.190 --> 03:08.532
Ask supports the same investigation with cited answers from the approved
corpus and can refuse when the evidence is absent.

03:08.532 --> 03:13.670
Verified establishes provenance, not truth, admissibility, disclosure
significance, legality or guilt.

03:14.670 --> 03:22.043
Evidential weight, investigative judgement, disclosure obligations,
proportionality, public interest and operational context cannot be

03:22.043 --> 03:24.677
delegated to a language model.

03:24.677 --> 03:32.577
Authorised investigators, disclosure officers, supervisors and accountable
officials determine what applies and what action follows.

03:32.577 --> 03:36.263
Prosecutors and courts retain their independent roles.

03:36.263 --> 03:44.690
Cortessa does not identify guilt, prioritise suspects, direct deployment,
authorise coercive action, make charging recommendations or

03:44.690 --> 03:46.270
decide judicial outcomes.

03:47.270 --> 03:55.927
An authorised user's approved revision can carry its signed identity, content
hash, parent lineage and approved audit context through

03:55.927 --> 04:00.484
the relevant departmental node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

04:00.484 --> 04:08.686
Conflicting branches and missing ancestry remain explicit; the hub cannot
publish another person's approval or choose the governing

04:08.686 --> 04:09.141
account.

04:09.141 --> 04:15.976
Receipt does not certify evidence, supersede the local corpus or make a record
searchable automatically.

04:15.976 --> 04:22.355
The receiving user governs import and use under existing case, disclosure and
handling controls.

04:22.355 --> 04:29.190
The local Ledger supports inspection but never replaces the formal evidential,
disclosure or decision record.

04:30.190 --> 04:35.310
Begin with one closed, synthetic, public or explicitly cleared workflow.

04:35.310 --> 04:41.454
Agree the corpus, roles, access boundary, baseline and evidence standard
before testing.

04:41.454 --> 04:48.622
Include missing records, amendments, ambiguous chronology, difficult scans and
questions that should be refused.

04:48.622 --> 04:56.814
Measure time to the governing source, citation completeness, reviewer effort,
accepted and rejected candidates, appropriate refusals,

04:56.814 --> 04:59.886
access-control behaviour and sampled source-path reproducibility.

04:59.886 --> 05:02.958
Then test one governed departmental exchange.

05:02.958 --> 05:08.590
These are evaluation hypotheses, not claimed operational, investigative or
justice outcomes.

05:09.590 --> 05:17.093
Bring one appropriately controlled policy, case-review or disclosure workflow
and the people authorised to judge it.

05:17.093 --> 05:23.189
Test the local evidence route and one permission-scoped departmental exchange
before considering expansion.

05:23.189 --> 05:30.223
Cortessa claims no policing customer, deployment, completed site rollout,
accreditation, evidential outcome, operational benefit or

05:30.223 --> 05:31.160
justice outcome.

05:31.160 --> 05:36.319
The architecture must be demonstrated and assured in a representative
environment.

05:36.319 --> 05:40.070
Start a conversation about a scoped policing evaluation.
